  "structural_interpretation": "The block masking G3 failure in linear/seed=123 is STRUCTURAL and SEED-SPECIFIC. It does not resolve with more epochs (200\u2192300\u2192500: -0.0670\u2192-0.0375\u2192-0.0132). Seeds 42 and 456 pass block masking with positive margins. Hypothesis: seed=123 generates a specific linear panel where the true graph structure introduces noise that hurts block-missing imputation, while the permuted graph decouples the sectors and relies more on temporal features (which are informative for block missing). This is a known limitation: graph-augmented models can hurt on block missing when the graph propagates incorrect prior beliefs about sector co-movement.",
